WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:08.760
Farm businesses have enjoyed
exceptionally high prices and incomes over

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:12.780
the last ten years. Even this year, with
somewhat lower crop and livestock prices,

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:17.640
farm cash incomes are well above their
long-run average. In fact, since the early

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:22.109
1980s, households that own and operate
farm businesses have consistently

00:00:22.109 --> 00:00:26.070
enjoyed higher incomes than the average
American household. This is not your

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:30.000
great-grandmother's poverty-riven
"Grapes of Wrath" farming community.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.050
Nevertheless, Congress continues to
funnel over twenty billion dollars a

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:38.280
year in subsidies to farm businesses.
Those payments mainly flow to the

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:42.480
largest farm operations, whose owners
enjoy incomes in the hundreds of

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:46.980
thousands of dollars. Many farm subsidy
programs also waste scarce economic

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:50.879
resources. For example, crop insurance
programs encourage farms to adopt

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:56.340
high-risk strategies and farm fragile
lands. Several conservation subsidies are

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:00.570
so poorly targeted that they have almost
no impact on the environment. So is there

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:05.189
any justification for continuing most
farm subsidy programs? The answer, quite

00:01:05.189 --> 00:01:07.540
simply, is no.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:12.900
So what do you think about
farm subsidies? Let us know in your

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:17.180
comments, and also let us know what other
topics you'd like our scholars to cover

00:01:17.189 --> 00:01:22.740
in 60 seconds. And be sure to like and
subscribe for more research and videos

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:26.270
from AEI

